Pantheon Prime — Silent Guitar v3

Words · Sentences · Sounds · Silences · Meaning

Danger, meet discernment. ;) 🤜🏻

I’ve turned the Silent Guitar into an actual playable instrument, rather than another set of instructions to build one.

The six strings encode E–C–A–D–O–R. The player supplies U.

The new instrument accepts sentences, transforms written words into melodic contours, treats animal calls as sound effects, and gives pauses their own symbols and timing.

The crucial distinction is preserved: saying meow, making a meowing sound, and leaving an empty place for a meow are three different operations.

I tested the browser interface: it renders all 26 silence types, composes sentence scores, and responds to string adjustments without runtime errors. The Python interpreter also passes 89 local checks.

